# NODX TUI And Desktop Showcase {#tui-showcase}

This companion showcase focuses on text-first surfaces: terminal rendering,
desktop preview, code blocks, notes, page breaks, speaker notes, and fallback
content that must remain useful without CSS.

:::toc {#local-map role="primary" depth="2" title="Document map"}
:::

## Operational Notes {#notes}

:::note {#review-note type="warning"}
Warnings should remain readable as plain text in terminal, desktop, and
accessibility-oriented renderers.
:::

- [x] Parse source bytes
- [x] Validate semantic constraints
- [x] Render TUI safely
- [ ] Complete external editor integrations

## Literal Blocks {#literal}

:::code {lang="sh"}
target/debug/nodx validate examples/showcase-tui.nodx
target/debug/nodx tui examples/showcase-tui.nodx
:::

:::quote {#quote}
Fallback text is not a second-class path. It is the portable document path.
:::

## Presentation Fallback {#presentation}

:::slide {#slide-1 title="Text-first slide" fallback="children"}
### Text-first slide {#slide-heading}

Slide-like content should still be visible as a structured section when a host
does not implement presentation behavior.

:::speaker-notes
Speaker notes are deferred presentation semantics, but terminal and desktop
views should keep them inspectable as text.
:::
:::

